

# Normally, the guideline is to remove Cargo.lock from gitignore if creating an executable, leave it for libraries.
# More information here https://doc.rust-lang.org/cargo/guide/cargo-toml-vs-cargo-lock.html
# But for nix + naersk we need to include it explicitly
!Cargo.lock

# Generated by Cargo, will have compiled files and executables
debug/
target/
tests/cargo-fmt/**/target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by nix / direnv
/result
.direnv/
